epsMaker
========

Turns the multiplot canvas into postscript. canvasDraw.c renders every canvas
item in a series of phases (reading data, deciding axis ranges, typesetting all
text with LaTeX in one run, and writing postscript), then converts the result
to the output format of the current terminal. Each type of canvas item has its
own eps_*.c file; graphs are drawn by the eps_plot*.c files.

bmp_a85.c, bmp_a85.h
    Encodes binary data, such as images, in postscript's ASCII85 format.

bmp_bmpread.c, bmp_bmpread.h
    Reads Windows and OS/2 bitmap (BMP) images, including run-length encoded
    ones, for the image command.

bmp_gifread.c, bmp_gifread.h
    Reads GIF images, decompressing their LZW-encoded data, for the image
    command.

bmp_image.h
    The bitmap_data structure which describes an image, and constants for its
    color type and compression.

bmp_jpegread.c, bmp_jpegread.h
    Reads JPEG images without decompressing them, so that their compressed data
    can be embedded directly in postscript.

bmp_optimise.c, bmp_optimise.h
    Reduces the size of images, by converting them to paletted or greyscale
    form and packing several pixels into each byte where possible.

bmp_pngread.c, bmp_pngread.h
    Reads PNG images using libpng, for the image command.

canvasDraw.c, canvasDraw.h
    Draws the whole canvas: calls each item's handler in each phase, runs
    LaTeX, writes the final postscript file with its prolog and embedded fonts,
    and converts it to other formats or sends it to a viewer.

dvi_font.c, dvi_font.h
    Loads the fonts used in LaTeX's output: reads TeX font metric files and
    finds the Type 1 fonts which draw them, using the dvips font map.

dvi_interpreter.c, dvi_interpreter.h
    Interprets the operators of LaTeX's dvi output, writing postscript which
    draws the same text, one page per piece of text on the canvas.

dvi_read.c, dvi_read.h
    Reads dvi files operator by operator, passing each to the interpreter.

eps_arrow.c, eps_arrow.h
    Draws arrow and line canvas items, and provides the arrow-drawing routine
    used elsewhere.

eps_box.c, eps_box.h
    Draws box canvas items.

eps_circle.c, eps_circle.h
    Draws circle and arc canvas items.

eps_comm.h
    The EPSComm structure, which carries the state of the rendering process
    between all of the functions in this directory.

eps_core.c, eps_core.h
    Sets line and fill colors, line widths and line types, writing postscript
    only when they change, and tracks the bounding box of what has been drawn.

eps_ellipse.c, eps_ellipse.h
    Draws ellipse canvas items.

eps_eps.c, eps_eps.h
    Includes existing encapsulated postscript files in the output, for the eps
    command.

eps_image.c, eps_image.h
    Includes bitmap images in the output, for the image command.

eps_piechart.c, eps_piechart.h
    Draws pie charts, with their labels and keys.

eps_plot.c, eps_plot.h
    Draws graphs: reads their data, samples their functions, collects their
    text, and draws their datasets, axes, grids, legends, labels and arrows.

eps_plot_axespaint.c, eps_plot_axespaint.h
    Draws the axes of graphs, with their ticks and labels.

eps_plot_canvas.c, eps_plot_canvas.h
    Maps values on a graph's axes to positions on the page, including the
    projection of three-dimensional graphs.

eps_plot_colormap.c, eps_plot_colormap.h
    Draws the colormap plot style as a bitmap image, and the color scales
    beside graphs.

eps_plot_contourmap.c, eps_plot_contourmap.h
    Draws the contourmap plot style, tracing and labelling lines of constant
    value through gridded data.

eps_plot_filledregion.c, eps_plot_filledregion.h
    Fills regions bounded by paths through data points, clipped to the edges of
    the graph.

eps_plot_gridlines.c, eps_plot_gridlines.h
    Draws the grid lines of graphs.

eps_plot_labelsarrows.c, eps_plot_labelsarrows.h
    Draws the arrows and text labels placed on graphs with "set arrow" and "set
    label".

eps_plot_legend.c, eps_plot_legend.h
    Lays out and draws the legends (keys) of graphs.

eps_plot_linedraw.c, eps_plot_linedraw.h
    Draws lines through series of data points, clipping them to the edges of
    the graph.

eps_plot_linkedaxes.c, eps_plot_linkedaxes.h
    Handles axes linked to other axes, propagating ranges along the links,
    including through "using" expressions.

eps_plot_styles.c, eps_plot_styles.h
    Draws datasets in each plot style, and their legend icons; assigns default
    styles to successive datasets, and widens axis ranges to include the data.

eps_plot_threedimbuff.c, eps_plot_threedimbuff.h
    A buffer which sorts the postscript of three-dimensional graphs by depth,
    so that nearer items hide further ones.

eps_plot_ticking.c, eps_plot_ticking.h
    Decides the final range of each axis, and where its ticks go, and generates
    tick labels.

eps_plot_ticking_auto.c, eps_plot_ticking_auto.h
    Places ticks automatically on axes which are non-linear or have format
    expressions, by sampling the labels along the axis.

eps_plot_ticking_auto2.c, eps_plot_ticking_auto2.h
    Places ticks automatically on ordinary linear and logarithmic axes.

eps_plot_ticking_auto3.c, eps_plot_ticking_auto3.h
    Places ticks on an axis linked to another axis of the same length, by
    copying that axis's ticks.

eps_point.c, eps_point.h
    Draws point canvas items, with their labels.

eps_polygon.c, eps_polygon.h
    Draws polygon canvas items.

eps_settings.c, eps_settings.h
    Dimensions used throughout postscript output, such as the default line
    width and the sizes of arrowheads and ticks, which can be scaled from the
    configuration file.

eps_style.c, eps_style.h
    The dash patterns of line types, and the postscript procedures which draw
    point and star types.

eps_text.c, eps_text.h
    Draws text canvas items.

kpse_wrap.c, kpse_wrap.h
    Finds TeX's font files, using the kpathsea library or by asking kpsewhich
    where TeX looks for them.
